ght before this election  was yeah de la we being invited to Saudi  Arabia she was and trying to strengthen  his his relationships with some of the  Arab powers so what will some of those  neighbors Jordan Syria Saudi Arabia Iran  what will they be looking for well  they're all be looking for something  different and they all put a ton of  money into the campaigns because they  all had their candidates you know this  is a region where everybody watches  everybody else and if you're weak you  can expect that your neighbors are going  to dabble which is what happened I think  they are the neighbors are going to be  watching for a coalition that emerges  that makes the country more stable and  that will tell them where Iraq is headed  if there is some power sharing in the  region what it means to ear ox Sunni  neighbors is that Iraq is going to go it  alone they won't be an Iranian proxy and  that will be important to Saudi Arabia  to Egypt to Jordan and even to Turkey in  some ways I think what the Iranians are  going to watch for is that the bath is  what they consider the Sunnis aren't too  strong

